      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think \"wildcard rule\" is a good name within ConnectivityService. It\u0027s too vague.\n\nWe could rename this to requiresWildcardVpnRule, but... \"wildcard rule\" is not really a concept in itself - it\u0027s the same as the VPN allow rule, except it allows packets on all interfaces. What if we did something like the following?\n\n    @Nullable\n    private String getVpnIsolationInterface(@NonNull NetworkAgentInfo nai,\n            @NonNull NetworkCapabilities nc, LinkProperties lp) {\n        if (nc \u003d\u003d null || lp \u003d\u003d null) return null;\n        if (nai.isVPN()\n                \u0026\u0026 !nai.networkAgentConfig.allowBypass\n                \u0026\u0026 nc.getOwnerUid() !\u003d Process.SYSTEM_UID\n                \u0026\u0026 lp.getInterfaceName() !\u003d null\n                \u0026\u0026 (lp.hasIpv4DefaultRoute() || lp.hasIpv4UnreachableDefaultRoute())\n                \u0026\u0026 (lp.hasIpv6DefaultRoute() || lp.hasIpv6UnreachableDefaultRoute())\n                \u0026\u0026 !lp.hasExcludeRoute()) {\n            return lp.getInterfaceName();\n        }\n        return null;\n    }\n\n    private boolean requiresVpnAllowRule(NetworkAgentInfo nai, LinkProperties lp,\n            String filterIface {\n        // Only filter if nai has an interface.\n        if (lp \u003d\u003d null || lp.getInterfaceName() \u003d\u003d null) return false;\n        // Before T, allow rules are only needed if VPN isolation is enabled.\n        // After T, allow rules are needed for all VPNs.\n        return filterIface !\u003d null || nai.isVPN() \u0026\u0026 SdkLevel.isAtLeastT());\n    }\n\nI think it might simplify the code. in updateVpnFiltering you\u0027d have\n\n        final String oldIface \u003d getVpnIsolationInterface(\n                nai, nai.networkCapabilities, oldLp);\n        final String newIface \u003d getVpnIsolationInterface(\n                nai, nai.networkCapabilities, newLp);\n        final boolean wasFiltering \u003d requiresVpnAllowRule(nai, oldIface);\n        final boolean needsFiltering \u003d requiresVpnAllowRule(nai, newIface);\n\n        if (!wasFiltering \u0026\u0026 !needsFiltering) {\n            // Nothing to do.\n            return;\n        }\n\n        if (Objects.equals(oldIface, newIface) \u0026\u0026 (wasFiltering \u003d\u003d needsFiltering)) {\n            // Nothing changed.\n            return;\n        }\n\nThoughts?\n\nIf this seems like a good idea, it might make sense to do it in its own separate refactoring change (minus the isAtLeastT() code) to see if it passes the existing unit tests.",
