      "side": 1,
      "message": "What you have here is basically a multiset, and it might be useful elsewhere. I think it might be worth extracting this code from this method into a simple static inner class. That would make it easier to reuse, unit test, etc. in the future. Something like:\n\n    private static class MultiSet\u003cT\u003e {\n        private Map\u003cT, Integer\u003e mMap \u003d new ArrayMap\u003c\u003e();\n\n        /** returns true iff the set did not previously contain the element */\n        boolean add(T key) {\n            final int count \u003d mMap.getOrDefault(key, 0);\n            mMap.put(key, count + 1);\n            return count \u003d\u003d 0;\n        }\n\n        /** returns true iff the set does not contain the element */\n        boolean remove(T key) [\n            final int count \u003d mMap.getOrDefault(key, 0);\n            if (count \u003d\u003d 0) {\n                // log an error?\n                return true;\n            } else if (count \u003d\u003d 1) {\n                mMap.remove(key);\n                return true;\n            } else {\n                mMap.put(count - 1);\n                return false;\n            }\n        }\n\n        boolean contains(T key) {\n            return mMap.contains(key);\n        }\n    }",
